      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DON JACKO (1) has made a good start to his career. Placed in his fist three outings then finished fourth from the back row at his latest appearance at this circuit and distance. Suited dropping to maiden grade and the ace draw gives him every chance to break through. SWEET PERFECTION (7) was well fancied and led but found one better on debut at this circuit and distance, boxing on well to finish 2.3 metres behind the winner. May need luck at some stage extracting from the inside of the second row but is open to natural improvement. LOMBOSATTITUDE (3) draws well and is looming as a threat after a better effort last start, beaten just a head when second at Newcastle. REVERSE SWING (9) faces the starter for the first time. By King Of Swing and hails from the Joe Conolly stable. Tricky draw but has shown enough at the trials to be competitive.",
